SUMMARY:Get Wild: FALLing for Trees!
DESCRIPTION:Join TLC for this family friendly exploration of the wonderful world of trees!\nTrail Guide Donna Agnew will lead families on a romp through Old Creedmoor Nature Preserve to explore the life cycle of trees\, go on a tree scavenger hunt\, search for cool bugs and plants\, and make nature leaf crowns! \n\nFilled with Umbrella Magnolias\, Sparklberry trees\, and so much more\, Old Creedmoor is the perfect spot for exploring trees. Perfect for kids ages 5+ and their grownups! This event is free\, but pre-registration is required:\n\n\n\nIf registration is full\, please email Meera Butalia at mbutalia@triangleland.org to be added to the waitlist.
URL:https://triangleland.org/event/get-wild-falling-for-trees
LOCATION:Old Creedmoor Nature Preserve\, 13509 Old Creedmoor Rd\, Wake Forest\, NC\, 27587\, United States
END:VEVENT
