SUMMARY:Trail Talks with TLC: Williamson
DESCRIPTION:Join TLC staff for guided nature journaling at Williamson Nature Preserve!\nSlow down and connect with nature with Senior Volunteer and Outreach Associate\, Amaya Horner! Amaya will give a brief history of Williamson Nature Preserve and talk about the types of programs that this working farm and public preserve offers. Then\, we will navigate Two Ponds Loop\, making stops along the way to collect observations about the world around us using nature journaling methods curated by naturalist and educator\, John Muir Laws.\n\nPlease bring your own journal and writing utensils\, but we will have some extra materials on hand. Participants will receive a Quick Start Guide to Nature Journaling zine written by John Muir Laws and the Wild Wonder Foundation to take home! This will be a slow\, 1.5 mile hike on uneven terrain. Bring a full water bottle and a mat or blanket to sit on for the still moments on trail.  This event is free\, but preregistration is required.\n\n 
URL:https://triangleland.org/event/trail-talks-with-tlc-williamson
LOCATION:Williamson Farm and Nature Preserve\, 4429 Old Country Mial Rd\, Raleigh\, 27610\, United States
ORGANIZER;CN="Amaya Horner":MAILTO:ahorner@triangleland.org
END:VEVENT
