SUMMARY:Nature Storytime: Forest Detectives
DESCRIPTION:Become a Forest Detective at our monthly Nature Storytime!\nEngage your sense of smell\, sight\, sound\, and wonder! This month’s story time will invite everyone to learn about the cycles and secrets of nature through nature stories\, nature games\, and a short ramble through the Brumley Nature Preserve. Join a TLC educator for this monthly story series where you can meet other families in your community and learn about nature. This month's nature stories are: "All Around Us" By Xelena Gomez and "Beneath" by Cori Doerrfeld. This program is designed for kids age 3-7 and their grownups. Please register all members of the family attending\, including children and adults. This event is free\, but preregistration is required:
URL:https://triangleland.org/event/nature-storytime-forest-detectives-2
LOCATION:Brumley South Nature Preserve\, 3055 New Hope Church Rd\, Chapel Hill\, NC\, 27514\, United States
END:VEVENT
